      "lineNbr": 103,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-25T09:36:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It doesn\u0027t seem to be mapped to std::optional - the generated signature is right here and just passes a ScopedFileDescriptor.\nThe generated code (in out/soong/.intermediates/packages/modules/Virtualization/virtualizationservice/aidl/android.system.virtualizationservice-ndk-source/gen/android/system/virtualizationservice/) uses AParcel_readRequiredParcelFileDescriptor / AParcel_writeRequiredParcelFileDescriptor which explicitly don\u0027t allow -1, and -1 seems to be the value used to signal null. (See e.g. http://cs/android/frameworks/native/libs/binder/ndk/include_cpp/android/binder_parcel_utils.h?l\u003d242)\n\nThe documentation at https://source.android.com/devices/architecture/aidl/aidl-backends#nullability isn\u0027t very helpful unfortunately.\n\nI\u0027m not convinced @nullable is actually supported here.",
      "parentUuid": "2b99576a_cff8db04",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 103,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 103,
        "endChar": 62
